The bug is that the transformation assumes that an `insertelement` with a constant index is always within bounds or valid to scalarize. If the index is out of bounds, the instruction is effectively UB or poison, and scalarizing it without checking bounds can lead to incorrect optimization (e.g., removing UB or changing the semantics).

The fix is to ensure the insertion index is within the bounds of the vector type, but only for fixed-length vectors (where we can check the size at compile time). Scalable vectors are skipped to avoid breaking existing optimizations for scalable vector types.

